title>Critical roles of PPAR <inline-formula><mml:math id="M21"><mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b2;</mml:mi><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:mi>&#x003b4;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> in keratinocyte response to inflammation</article-title><source><italic>Genes &#x00026; Development</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><issue>24</issue><fpage>3263</fpage><lpage>3277</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11751632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Michalik</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Di-Poi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Desvergne</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wahli</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Critical roles of the nuclear receptor PPAR<inline-formula><mml:math id="M22"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b2;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> (peroxisome-proliferator-activated receptor <inline-formula><mml:math id="M23"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b2;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>) in skin wound healing</article-title><source><italic>Biochemical Society Transactions</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>32</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>102</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14748722</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Y-X</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>C-L</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Regulation of muscle fiber type and running endurance by PPAR<inline-formula><mml:math id="M24"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b4;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></in